# The Docker build context only needs the prebuilt binaries. Everything else is
# noise — keep the context tiny so `docker build` stays fast. The big
# testfixtures/resource-firebom*.json fixtures and logs alone are ~250MB.
#
# Every binary the Dockerfile COPYs MUST be un-ignored here, or `docker build`
# fails with "not found" even though the file exists in bin/ — `*` excludes it
# from the build context Docker sees.
*
# Binaries COPYd by the images built from the repo root. The lean control/broker image
# (root Dockerfile) uses converge + conctl; the full-tooling worker image
# (Dockerfile.stdworker) uses stdworker; the classic demo worker
# (examples/demos/classic/Dockerfile.classicworker) uses its own binary.
!bin/converge.linux-amd64
!bin/conctl.linux-amd64
!bin/stdworker.linux-amd64
!bin/classic-worker.linux-amd64
# The stdworker image's entrypoint (Dockerfile.stdworker COPYs it from the repo root).
!stdworker-entrypoint.sh
